<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Katzenelnbogen</h1><p class="st-meta">1095 CE – 1479 CE (approx.) · capital Rheinfels</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Rhineland county rich from tolls on the Rhine and the earliest Riesling vineyards, whose inheritance made the landgraves of Hesse a major power.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The counts of Katzenelnbogen first appear around 1095 as advocates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishopric-of-worms">Bishopric of Worms</a> and the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorsch">Lorsch</a>. They built Katzenelnbogen castle in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taunus">Taunus</a> and expanded into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> valley, acquiring lands on both banks and the area of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts became wealthy from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> tolls collected at castles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rheinfels-castle">Rheinfels</a> above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sankt-goar">Sankt Goar</a>, built in 1245, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burg-katz">Burg Katz</a>. Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-iv-count-of-katzenelnbogen">Johann IV</a> is linked with the first recorded mention of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riesling">Riesling</a> grapes, in 1435. Their lands stretched from the Rhine into the upper Rhine plain.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-i-count-of-katzenelnbogen">Philipp the Elder</a>, the last count, died in 1479, his daughter's husband, Landgrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-landgrave-of-hesse">Henry III of Hesse</a>, inherited the county. Its rich tolls helped make <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> a significant power; the upper county around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> later became the core of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Hesse-Darmstadt</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-katzenelnbogen.jpg" alt="County of Katzenelnbogen" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume de L'Isle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Katzenelnbogen_country.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1095 CE – 1479 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rheinfels</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Johann IV of Katzenelnbogen, Philipp the Elder</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Rhine Franconian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Katzenelnbogen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1287&amp;focus=county-of-katzenelnbogen" aria-label="County of Katzenelnbogen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4862 430 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Katzenelnbogen lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5182 686L5229 694M5182 686L5215 656"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5215 656h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5182 686h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5182 686h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1287&amp;focus=county-of-katzenelnbogen">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
